  "question": {
    "text": "Water is flowing in streamline motion through a horizontal tube. The pressure at a point in the tube is $p$ where the velocity of flow is $v$. At another point, where the pressure is $p / 2,$ the velocity of flow is [density of water $=\\rho]$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "jhDUY",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{v^{2}+\\frac{p}{\\rho}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Sgk5j",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{v^{2}-\\frac{p}{\\rho}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FcC0d",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{v^{2}+\\frac{2 p}{\\rho}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "HzKnj",
      "text": "$\\sqrt{v^{2}-\\frac{2 p}{\\rho}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As the water is flowing through the horizontal tube, so in the streamline flow of water, the sun of static pressure and dynamic pressure is constant $i, e$\r\n$$\r\nP+\\frac{1}{2} \\rho v^{2}=\\frac{P}{2}+\\frac{1}{2} \\rho v_{1}^{2}\r\n$$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad v_{1}=\\sqrt{\\frac{P}{\\rho}+v^{2}}$",
    "image": null
  },
